From 3c1838a1b03d61df1c3ce203d03293dbec75e35c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:37:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 151/171] rule-set: an answer "not modified" writes the time
 alone to the cache file

On a 304 a remote rule set loaded its whole saved list from the cache file
and saved it again, only to change its time: the list written once per
update_interval to a cache file that may be on flash (podkop keeps it
there to survive a reboot), a few MB per list.

The cache file keeps that time apart, in the bucket rule_set_checked: a
304 writes eight bytes. A start takes the later of the time of the saved
content and that one. A sing-box without the bucket deletes it at its
start and reads the time of the content, as before; a cache file that
does not keep the times (adapter.RuleSetCheckCache) saves the set again.
